 add('multiplayer','matchmaking','Find a public match and keep the room moving','<ol><li>Use a registered trainer account. The .73 notes say Guests are directed to account creation; this guide cannot inspect or migrate your session.</li><li>Choose Find a match, then a mode, duo/trio/squad, map and difficulty, or Any. Matching first prefers your region.</li><li>The crowned leader chooses the map and starts when the room is ready. A friends’ room can enable Find teammates.</li><li>After a match, return to the room to regroup. An inactive public leader leaves after 90 seconds and the next player leads; an idle lone search cancels after three minutes.</li><li>Use the signal wheel: hold G, or L3 on a controller; tapping G marks the looked-at position. The current big-map binding defaults to R3 and can be changed.</li></ol><p>Upgrade-choice protection is finite: five seconds per level, capped at ten, without automatic refill. These are source-described rules, not a completed public match.</p><p><a href="/pokebonk/team-survival/">Prepare for Team Survival →</a></p>')
 p=pages[P+'multiplayer/'];c=cite(p);p['html']=p['html'].replace('<article class="prose">','<article class="prose"><p class="note"><strong>October 29 · original .75:</strong> Current co-op requires a registered trainer account. Read the public-matchmaking and signal-wheel rules below; older Guest or controller instructions do not override them.'+c+'</p>',1)
